The following files contain portions adapted from pi-dynamic-workflows by Michael Liverant,
obtained via the fork github.com/tyroneross/pi-dynamic-workflows-fork (source repository:
github.com/Michaelliv/pi-dynamic-workflows), used under the MIT License:

  core/workstream-lint.mjs
    (a) DETERMINISM_BLOCKLIST — the regex that rejects Date.now() / Math.random() / new Date()
        in declared commands, ensuring a shared plan is reproducible across agents.
    (b) Literal-descriptor validation discipline — the evaluateLiteral/validateMeta pattern that
        validates every required field as a plain JSON value, never executing it.

  core/limiter.mjs
    (c) createLimiter — the bounded-concurrency helper that lets a host cap its own fan-out.

  core/route.mjs
    (d) parallel() / pipeline() control-flow and the budget object — the deterministic-routing
        primitives, ported host-neutral (decoupled from pi's node:vm executor, WorkflowAgent, and
        agent() primitive) and extended for the durable model (onError/abort visibility; generic
        budget units, not pi's token heuristic).

